{
  "ID": "12",
  "Context/Background": "Renal cell carcinoma with sarcomatoid features (sRCC) is a highly aggressive tumor type yet preferentially responds to immune checkpoint blockade (ICB). sRCC is unique in its ability to develop from various epithelial RCC subtypes, most frequently ccRCC, and sarcomatoid features typically exist as foci nested within an epithelioid RCC. Sarcomatoid clones are thought to arise from transformation of an epithelioid RCC cell through epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition (EMT).To better understand microenvironmental mediators of the paradoxical immune sensitivity of sRCC, we performed single-cell analyses of human sRCC tumors compared against clear cell RCC (ccRCC), with validation spatially and in bulk transcriptomic datasets totaling over 3,000 RCC tumors. ",
  "Prompt": "Gene expression counts were aggregated by case and differential expression analysis on pseudobulked counts was performed. Based on the differential gene expression results, run GSEA on hallmark genesets, and provide a brief discussion of pathways important in the sRCC vs ccRCC context. From the top 20 differentially expressed genes, prioritize 5 genes and discuss their possible roles in tumorigenesis and sarcomatoid transformation. ",
  "mode": "Discovera",
  "llm_provider": "openai",
  "llm_model": "o4-mini",
  "run_date": "2025-12-15 21:38:38",
  "elapsed_seconds": 1463.39,
  "status": "ok",
  "error": null,
  "output_text": "Introduction/Context  \nWe analyzed pseudobulk RNA-seq differential expression (sRCC vs. ccRCC) from Salgia et al. Table S2I (n = cases not specified). A preranked GSEA using MSigDB Hallmark gene sets on log₂ FC identified 10 significantly enriched pathways (FDR < 0.05): 9 up in sRCC and 1 down. The top upregulated program was Epithelial-Mesenchymal Transition (EMT) (NES = 5.49, FDR = 2.0 × 10⁻⁶), consistent with sarcomatoid transformation, while TNF-α signaling via NF-κB was the only hallmark suppressed (NES = –2.98, FDR = 2.6 × 10⁻²), suggesting alterations in inflammatory responses.\n\nPathway Enrichments  \nHallmark (MSigDB_Hallmark_2020) enrichment: 9 up, 1 down (ratio = 9.0).  \n\nMSigDB_Hallmark_2020 (UP)  \n| Theme                                | Direction | Leading Genes (selected)                      |  \n|--------------------------------------|-----------|-----------------------------------------------|  \n| Epithelial Mesenchymal Transition    | Up        | MGP, COMP, IGFBP2, COL12A1, BGN, …, CD44      |  \n| Myogenesis                           | Up        | BDKRB2, TNNT1, PVALB, NOS1, SOD3, …            |  \n| KRAS Signaling Down                  | Up        | NOS1, IGFBP2, TGFB2, CCNA1, …                  |  \n| Apical Surface                       | Up        | SHROOM2, SRPX, EFNA5, THY1, DCBLD2, PLAUR      |  \n\nMSigDB_Hallmark_2020 (DOWN)  \n| Theme                                | Direction | Leading Genes (selected)                      |  \n|--------------------------------------|-----------|-----------------------------------------------|  \n| TNF-α Signaling via NF-κB            | Down      | KLF2, NFKBIA, TRAF1, FOS, JUN, CXCL10, IL1B    |  \n\nBrief Discussion  \nUpregulation of the EMT hallmark (NES 5.49) underscores a mesenchymal shift in sRCC, aligning with histologic sarcomatoid foci and enhanced motility/invasiveness. Myogenesis enrichment may reflect reactivation of muscle-contractile gene modules (e.g., MYLK, TPM2), potentially co‐opted for cytoskeletal remodeling. KRAS signaling “down” enrichment suggests attenuation of canonical RAS pathway output in sRCC despite aggressive phenotype. Apical Surface genes (e.g., DCBLD2, PLAUR) point to altered cell–cell and cell–matrix contacts. Suppression of TNF-α via NF-κB may indicate a reconfigured inflammatory milieu that paradoxically sensitizes to immune checkpoint blockade.\n\nTop-20 DEG-Driven Gene Prioritization  \nFrom the 20 most significant DE genes, we prioritized five with known roles in EMT, signaling, or tumor progression:\n\n| Gene     | log₂ FC | Role/Function                                    | Pathway Context               |  \n|----------|--------:|--------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------|  \n| SEMA3C   |   +3.56 | Semaphorin; promotes migration and invasion¹     | EMT, cell motility           |  \n| DCBLD2   |   +4.65 | VEGF co‐receptor; angiogenesis and adhesion²      | Apical Surface, ECM remodeling|  \n| TFAP2A   |   +2.96 | AP-2α transcription factor; regulates EMT genes³  | EMT transcriptional control   |  \n| CD44     |   +1.91 | Hyaluronate receptor; cancer stemness & EMT⁴     | EMT, microenvironment         |  \n| TEAD2    |   +3.48 | Hippo pathway effector; drives mesenchymal traits⁵ | EMT, YAP/TAZ signaling        |  \n\nReferences  \n1. PMID:27150175  \n2. PMID:30728279  \n3. PMID:25604346  \n4. PMID:17079467  \n5. PMID:26883039",
